``Detector.to_dict`` and the detector pickle no longer write a ``"hierarchy"`` entry for a single panel detector, so its geometry now appears in one place only. Dictionaries and pickles that contain one are still read. A new ``Detector.has_hierarchy()`` tells you whether a detector has a meaningful hierarchy, rather than the placeholder root node that every detector owns; use it in place of ``hasattr(detector, "hierarchy")``, which is always true.
